  "summary": "An experienced IT professional with 34 years of experience developing enterprise applications using COBOL, CICS, Datacom, and Microsoft SQL. Particularly skilled in inbound and outbound data transmissions (EDI, Industry standard and client specific data formats).\n\nRecipient of Corporate Systems Employee Excellence Award \n\n15 years of working with Workers Comp Medical Bills \n          - Medical Bill Intake\n          - Adjudication\n          - Check and EOB Printing\n          - State Reporting \n\n8 years as Lead Developer of Medical Bill State Reporting to Florida, Texas, California, and Oregon\n \n8 years of experience working with Workers Comp Insurance Claims  \n \t- Inbound Data Transmissions\n\t- Batch Reporting\n\t- Claim Valuation (As of Point in Time)\n\t- Frequency and Cost Rankings\n\t- Check Printing\n\n1 year of experience working with ETL (Extract, Transform, Load) systems that used a variety of software tools \n  - SSIS\n\t- Visual Basic Scripts\n  - FTP\n\t- Microsoft SQL\n\t- Pervasive  \n\nRe-wrote several COBOL processes to dramatically improve performance and accuracy.\n\nMaintained large scale batch printing processes using COBOL and Xerox DJDE statements producing 3 to 20 million print images a month.\n\nWorked with batch printing process to interface with Documerge for Check and Medical Bill EOB printing.\n\nClient focused\nSuccessfully developed a rapport with clients and third-party vendors.",
